WEBVTT

00:07:26.275 --> 00:07:30.279
When a men's segment fell flat,
the problem was us.

00:07:30.321 --> 00:07:31.655
We would redo it.

00:07:32.198 --> 00:07:35.701
"Alright, come on, do your homework.
Pick it up. We're doing that again."

00:07:35.743 --> 00:07:38.287
When a segment
on women's sports fell flat,

00:07:38.287 --> 00:07:41.624
the problem was women's sports.

00:07:42.625 --> 00:07:47.213
This is a microcosm
for how this plays out across media.

00:07:48.005 --> 00:07:51.467
Never finding the new angle,
never finding the new story.

00:07:51.467 --> 00:07:52.718
So what you do

00:07:52.718 --> 00:07:56.305
is you rely on the millions of stories
that already exist.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.433
And you know what already exists?

00:07:59.475 --> 00:08:02.061
Every men's sports story imaginable.